# Generated figure outputs: regenerated independently on every machine that
# runs make_figures.py/plot_*.py, so every PDF/TIFF diverges and becomes an
# unresolvable binary merge conflict the moment two machines both commit them
# (see the 45-file conflict from ARC vs local on 2026-07-26). AGENTS.md already
# says plots should not be committed at all; this directory is the concrete
# case that broke `git pull` on ARC. *.png was already ignored above but not
# the PDF/TIFF/SVG formats savefig() also writes.
plots/figures/
plots/figures/**/*.pdf
plots/figures/**/*.tiff
plots/figures/**/*.svg

# Keep a discoverable figure destination in every clone (including ARC), but
# continue to ignore all generated binary/CSV outputs. Git tracks files, not
# empty directories, so the two README files are the portable placeholders.
!plots/figures/
plots/figures/*
!plots/figures/README.md
!plots/figures/benchmark/
plots/figures/benchmark/*
!plots/figures/benchmark/README.md

# Generated benchmark workspace. 9,047 of its 9,072 tracked files were
# per-protein inputs/ regenerated by the prepare stage, and results/ is
# rewritten by every evaluate run, so both machines diverge immediately.
# The small results CSVs are the only thing worth versioning; copy those to a
# tracked location deliberately rather than committing the whole workspace.
arc_benchmark/

# Never track the accidental top-level directory whose name is one space.
/\ /
